{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevUniquenessBoundedCapstone","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PhiBProd"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessAssembly.phiBProd_uniqueUpToScalar_of_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhiBProdUniquenessAssembly.phiBProd_uniqueUpToScalar_of_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhiBProdUniquenessAssembly.lean#L41-L72","doc":"**Concrete-`Φ_b` uniqueness (boundedness route).** For the explicit modular-double\nproduct `Φ_b = phiBProd (substrateB t)` (`t = ln q₀ > 0`), any `FaddeevPhi` solution `Φ₁`\nwhose normal-form ratio to `Φ_b` is **bounded** on `ℂ` (the state-integral endowment,\n`hbdd`) is a **scalar multiple** of `Φ_b` on `Φ_b`'s nonvanishing locus. The two structural\nhypotheses the generic capstone leaves open — that the reference is a `FaddeevPhi` solution\nand that its period lattice is nondegenerate — are **discharged here for the concrete\nproduct** (`faddeevPhi_phiBProd_substrate`, `substrateB_sq_im_pos`); only the analytic\nboundedness (plus the ratio/density bookkeeping) remains. ","signatureChunk":0}]}